{"content":[{"c":["AHOAH, AHOHI*, AHOHITE*"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["One of Bela’s nine sons, a member of Benjamin’s tribe (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.8.4","r":"1Chr.8.4","rawR":"1Chr.8.4","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.8.4","value":"1Chr.8.4"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 8:4"},"). Ahoah’s descendants were called Ahohites, and two of them were among King David’s most effective warriors: Dodo (“son of Ahohi,” ",{"href":"?bref=2Sam.23.9","r":"2Sam.23.9","rawR":"2Sam.23.9","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Sam.23.9","value":"2Sam.23.9"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Sm 23:9"},"; spelled “Dodai” in ",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.27.4","r":"1Chr.27.4","rawR":"1Chr.27.4","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.27.4","value":"1Chr.27.4"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 27:4"},") and Zalmon the Ahohite (",{"href":"?bref=2Sam.23.28","r":"2Sam.23.28","rawR":"2Sam.23.28","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Sam.23.28","value":"2Sam.23.28"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Sm 23:28"},"; called “Ilai” in ",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.11.29","r":"1Chr.11.29","rawR":"1Chr.11.29","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.11.29","value":"1Chr.11.29"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 11:29"},")."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"AhoahAhohiAhohite","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"1 Chr 8:4","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.8.4","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.8.4","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.8.4"},{"anchorText":"2 Sm 23:9","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Sam.23.9","rawQueryValue":"2Sam.23.9","sourceRefExact":"2Sam.23.9"},{"anchorText":"1 Chr 27:4","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.27.4","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.27.4","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.27.4"},{"anchorText":"2 Sm 23:28","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Sam.23.28","rawQueryValue":"2Sam.23.28","sourceRefExac